  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IND: DAHEJ LNG TERMINAL EXPANSION PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PLL owns and operates India&amp;apos;s first liquefied natural gas (LNG) import and regasification terminal, which started commercial operations on 9 April 2004. In the first phase, the terminal had a capacity of 5 million metric tons per annum (MMTPA). PLL imports LNG mainly from Ras Laffan Liquefied Natural Gas Company Limited (II) (Rasgas) in Qatar. PLL regasifies the LNG and sells to GAIL (India) Ltd., Indian Oil Corporation Ltd. (IOC) and Bharat Petroleum Corporation Ltd. (BPCL). GAIL, IOC, and BPCL in turn sell the gas to industrial end users. PLL has recently completed its expansion plan which has increased its capacity to 10 MMTPA.</narrative>
  </description>
